# The repository-root ignore file carries a Python template whose `lib/` rule was meant for a build
# directory — and which also matches this application's own `lib/` source directory at any depth.
# The modules already committed there are tracked, so the rule was invisible until a *new* file was
# added and git quietly refused to see it. Re-included here: a deeper ignore file overrides a
# shallower one, so this negation is what keeps `frontend/lib/` committable.
!lib/

# Task 21.8 manual-pass harness working directory (scripts/manual-pass-serve.sh).
.manual-pass/
